## 🟢 Revised Implementation Approach

### Schema Changes (Minimal)

```prisma
model CourseBundle {
  id          String             @id @default(cuid())
  title       String
  slug        String             @unique
  description String?
  price       Float              // must be > 0 and validated
  currency    String             @default("NGN")
  isActive    Boolean            @default(true)
  tutorId     String             // references Tutor.id (owner)
  createdAt   DateTime           @default(now())
  updatedAt   DateTime           @updatedAt

  tutor       Tutor              @relation(fields: [tutorId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  items       CourseBundleItem[]

  @@map("course_bundles")
}

model CourseBundleItem {
  id       String       @id @default(cuid())
  bundleId String
  courseId  String

  bundle   CourseBundle  @relation(fields: [bundleId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)
  course   Course        @relation(fields: [courseId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@unique([bundleId, courseId])
  @@map("course_bundle_items")
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> **No `bundleId` on Transaction needed.** Store it in the existing `metadata` JSON column — the same pattern used for `groupPurchaseId` and `mentorshipSessionId`. This avoids a schema migration on the heavily-used `Transaction` table.

### Checkout Flow (Reuse, Don't Rebuild)

```
Student clicks bundle link
  → GET /bundles/[slug] (landing page: shows courses, savings, CTA)
  → POST beginBundleCheckout(bundleSlug)
      1. Resolve bundle → courseIds
      2. Validate: bundle.isActive, all courses PUBLISHED, all belong to bundle.tutor
      3. Check enrollment: reject if student owns ANY course in bundle
      4. Override split rate: pass `bundleSplit: 0.75` into computeCheckoutTotals
      5. Compute line items per-course (proportional price distribution)
      6. Create Transaction + LineItems (same shape as regular checkout)
      7. Store { bundleId, bundleSlug } in metadata
      8. Initialize Paystack → redirect
  → Paystack callback → finalizePaystackByReference (UNCHANGED)
      - Reads courseIds from metadata
      - Creates enrollments for all courses ✅
      - Creates TutorEarnings from line items ✅
      - Credits wallet ✅
```

### Split Rate Fix (pricing.ts)

```ts
export const SPLIT_RATES = {
  normal: 0.2,
  tutorReferral: 0.5,
  platformPromo: 0.2,
  instructorPromo: 0.5,
  bundle: 0.75,         // ← NEW
};
```

Add a `purchaseType` parameter to `computeCheckoutTotals` so it knows to use the bundle rate instead of the normal rate. The `getSplitPercent` function gains a `if (purchaseType === 'bundle') return SPLIT_RATES.bundle;` branch at the top.

### Fix the `finalizePaystack.ts` splitPercent bug

```diff
- splitPercent: item.isReferralPurchase
-   ? 0.5
-   : item.promoType === "PLATFORM"
-     ? 0.2
-     : item.promoType === "INSTRUCTOR"
-       ? 0.5
-       : 0.2,
+ splitPercent: item.discountedPrice > 0
+   ? item.tutorShareAmount / item.discountedPrice
+   : 0,
```

This makes the finalize path **derive** the split from the already-computed amounts, eliminating the dual-source-of-truth bug.

